 "implementation_notes": [
  "Usable wells are read from D32's results file of the same run (hpsc_split_half_REAL.json, primary pool, usable true); if it is absent, D32's own table is rebuilt.",
  "Recording duration and window length follow D32: the plate file's last spike time, cut into 6 equal windows; a spike on a window edge starts the next window and the last spike ends window 5.",
  "The electrode set is the extractor's active rule (FeatureParams defaults, >= 5 spikes/min over the whole recording) applied to each electrode; noisy electrodes are not removed (D32 did not remove them either).",
  "A rate is defined when the set has at least one electrode; the floor makes an empty window defined, so 'defined in all six windows' means a non-empty set.",
  "SD(b) and the variances in the T3 share are sample statistics (ddof 1); the median of s is numpy's median.",
  "T1 and T2 use one bootstrap: one generator (seed 20261028), each resample drawing human then rat wells, the same draw order as D32's interval; the ratios are human / rat; a resample with a zero rat denominator would be dropped and counted as nonfinite.",
  "'Lies above 1' is read strictly: the interval's lower end must exceed 1.",
  "The quadratic check compares the quadratic fit's residual SD with its own ddof (3) against the line's (ddof 2), and 'more than a third' strictly (s_quad < 2/3 s); the share with both at ddof 2 is reported as a sensitivity.",
  "The wells-needed figures use D32's formula (5% two-sided, 80% power, 20% and 50% falls) on the SD of d_resid; the same formula on the SD of d of this windowed rate is given beside it.",
  "Not registered, reported for reading T3: with independent, equal-variance window values and no trend, var(d_trend)/var(d) = 27/35 (about 0.77), above T3's 0.5 threshold.",
  "The registered caveat flag is set on T1 and T3 only, as registered; the residual SD s of a straight line also absorbs any curvature, so when the trend is curved T2 measures curvature as well as scatter; the median residual SD of the quadratic fit (s_quad) is reported beside the check as the descriptive reading.",
  "Added after the first real-data run and labelled post hoc: the slope spread expected from s alone, and the split-half change with the first window dropped."
 ],
